WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.880
A made up case.

2
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.100
Tara is a District Collector.

3
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.400
After the floods, a relief list

4
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.760
reaches her desk:

5
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.240
families whose homes were

6
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.070
damaged.

7
00:00:10.636 --> 00:00:12.376
She reads it twice.

8
00:00:12.376 --> 00:00:14.196
One name is missing from the

9
00:00:14.196 --> 00:00:15.176
damage survey:

10
00:00:15.176 --> 00:00:18.516
Dhanraj, a man of means.

11
00:00:18.516 --> 00:00:20.716
Somehow, the list has made room

12
00:00:20.716 --> 00:00:22.046
for his means.

13
00:00:22.579 --> 00:00:24.679
The phone calls have begun.

14
00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:26.939
Everyone says the same thing:

15
00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:28.569
let it pass.

16
00:00:29.021 --> 00:00:30.241
The dilemma:

17
00:00:30.241 --> 00:00:32.281
whose name stays on the list,

18
00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:33.991
and who decides?

19
00:00:34.639 --> 00:00:35.819
Option A:

20
00:00:35.819 --> 00:00:38.619
let it pass, and keep the peace.

21
00:00:38.619 --> 00:00:40.119
Option B:

22
00:00:40.119 --> 00:00:42.319
strike the name quietly, and say

23
00:00:42.319 --> 00:00:44.519
nothing. Option C:

24
00:00:44.519 --> 00:00:46.439
check the survey, record the

25
00:00:46.439 --> 00:00:49.039
reason, and inform her senior.

26
00:00:49.039 --> 00:00:50.929
Pause here, and choose.

27
00:00:51.603 --> 00:00:53.483
Option A shares relief by

28
00:00:53.483 --> 00:00:55.523
influence. The Conduct Rules

29
00:00:55.523 --> 00:00:58.173
say: decide on merit alone.

30
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.100
Option B is right in result, but

31
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.460
leaves no record.

32
00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.580
Public decisions should be open,

33
00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.310
and answerable.

34
00:01:06.763 --> 00:01:08.983
Option C checks the facts,

35
00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:11.143
writes the reason, tells the

36
00:01:11.143 --> 00:01:13.183
senior, and shows the final

37
00:01:13.183 --> 00:01:14.073
list.

38
00:01:14.488 --> 00:01:16.228
A sound answer checks the

39
00:01:16.228 --> 00:01:18.748
survey, records the reason,

40
00:01:18.748 --> 00:01:21.288
informs the senior, and puts the

41
00:01:21.288 --> 00:01:23.038
list in public view.

42
00:01:24.172 --> 00:01:24.759
For GS4:

43
00:01:24.759 --> 00:01:27.612
relief by loss, not by name.

44
00:01:27.612 --> 00:01:30.332
Decide on merit, and keep the

45
00:01:30.332 --> 00:01:31.342
record open.

46
00:01:32.298 --> 00:01:34.418
By evening the list is pinned

47
00:01:34.418 --> 00:01:36.138
outside the office.

48
00:01:36.138 --> 00:01:38.898
The queue is long, but everyone

49
00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.028
in it has lost something.
